6. Common Preparation Mistakes

Candidates should avoid these common mistakes:

Memorizing practice answers without understanding the underlying concepts.

Ignoring official documentation.

Studying API features without trying practical implementations.

Overlooking security and responsible AI principles.

Ignoring MCP and external tool integration.

Skipping scenario-based exercises.

Not reviewing incorrect practice answers.

A balanced approach combining theory, practical implementation, and regular revision is more effective.

